      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In the past, it was generally considered that the window of curability had been missed in metastatic solid cancers. At present, novel evidence suggests that oligometastatic cancer might be amenable to a multimodal curative treatment, including ablation of the primary tumour. In this article, we summarise the indications, the controversies and future perspectives of local treatment in oligometastatic urological malignancies."},
